%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Three personas, one per direct stakeholder role in the Design Scenarios. Two residents: Jan, a former postal worker (HP-01), and Elena, who ran the post office counter (HP-02). Myra, the care worker Elena trusts (HP-03). All provisional: built from literature and group reasoning, not from interviews.

= Human Persona - Jan [HP-01] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-01
|Name|Jan, resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Built on ST-01, ST-02, PS-01.
|Elaborates|ST-01; ST-02 on Elena's walks
|Role in Scenario|Walks with Elena; misses her slip, stumbles while talking (DS-01).
|Task Demands|(((
1. Agree to go
1. Keep a story going
1. Talk and watch the path at once
1. Turn back in time
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|(((
Can: walk 20-30 minutes with a rollator; tell old stories vividly; answer yes or no; choose between two.

Cannot: recall this morning; notice a repeated story, or a partner's slip.

Moderate dementia. Hearing aid. Copes by laughing slips off and going on as before.
)))
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-01 Autonomy - goes out for own reasons: "I'm not a dog to be walked"
* HV-06 Social connectedness - misses the chats on the doorsteps
* HV-07 Identity - the post round
* HV-02 Dignity - plain talk, no fuss
* HV-03 Privacy - "What I tell Elena is between us"
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Their daughter (ST-03) visits monthly and wrote the life story with the coordinator. Elena (ST-02) lives two doors down. Myra (ST-04) works most afternoons.
|History and Experiences|Thirty years delivering post in a small town, on foot and by bike. Walked the dog twice a day until moving in.
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Settings agreed (RP-02): guide on walks alone, bridge only; word help, off; starters, the post round and football. Will not be tracked.

= Human Persona - Elena [HP-02] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-02
|Name|Elena, resident with dementia
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only. Built on ST-01, ST-02, PS-01, PS-02.
|Elaborates|ST-01; ST-02 on Jan's walks
|Role in Scenario|Walks with Jan; loses the thread and finds it again (DS-01). Walks alone with the guide as company; asks for Thomas (DS-02).
|Task Demands|(((
1. Find words; keep the thread
1. Recover from a slip without embarrassment
1. Live with the loss of Thomas
1. Keep going out
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|(((
Can: walk 30 minutes without aid; talk easily; notice her own slips.

Cannot: always find a word; retain that Thomas has died.

Aged 81; mild Alzheimer's disease. Copes by facing it ("My head's no good any more"), and is embarrassed by slips in company.
)))
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-02 Dignity - slips not remarked on
* HV-06 Social connectedness - lonely since Thomas died
* HV-08 Truthfulness - "Don't fob me off"
* HV-03 Privacy - keeps her diagnosis to herself
* HV-07 Identity - twenty-five years behind the counter
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Widowed last year. Her son lives abroad and calls on Sundays. Jan (ST-02) lives two doors down. Myra (ST-04) is her trusted person for Thomas.
|History and Experiences|Ran the post office counter in the same town as Jan, and knew half the town by name. Moved in this year.
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Settings agreed (RP-02): guide on walks alone, conversation partner; word help, after a wait ("give me a moment first"); starters, the counter and her garden. Off-limits with every partner: her diagnosis. Thomas's death: Myra only, as agreed with her son.

= Human Persona - Myra [HP-03] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HP-03
|Name|Myra, care worker
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Group reasoning only. Built on ST-04, PS-02.
|Elaborates|ST-04
|Role in Scenario|Clips on the guides (DS-01). Answers Elena's question about Thomas (DS-02).
|Task Demands|(((
1. Start walks without walking each one
1. Come quickly when called
1. Answer sensitive questions as agreed
1. Keep the relationship map current with the coordinator
)))
|Specific Capabilities and Needs|Knows the residents; trained in gentle redirection. Needs: few, meaningful alerts; agreed answers in one place.
|Values and Motivations|(((
* HV-08 Truthfulness - painful news told as agreed with the family
* HV-04 Safety - every resident back, unharmed
* HV-05 Well-being - residents out, and calm
* HV-03 Privacy - no timing of her own work
)))
|Social Network and Relationships|Several residents per shift. Works with the coordinator. Talks with families at visits.
|History and Experiences|Heard a colleague tell Elena "He's at work".
|Constraints and Privacy Considerations|Will not pass on news she has not agreed with the family. Will not accept frequent low-value alerts.
